# OpsConsole — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the values you need.
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# NOTHING here is required to boot: with no key the app still runs end to end and
# every check safely returns UNCERTAIN (design principle #1). A key is only
# needed for the AI observation / find steps to actually look at photos.
#
# The Gemini key can ALSO be set at runtime from the in-app Settings page, which
# writes it to data/config.json (git-ignored). The config file wins over these
# env vars when both are present. NEVER commit a real key.

# --- AI providers ---------------------------------------------------------
# OpsConsole supports MULTIPLE providers and MULTIPLE keys at once. Any keys set
# here are added to the pool alongside keys added on the Settings page; the
# inspector tries them in order and fails over (quota-limited/failing key → next).
#
# Each provider's key(s) are picked up from these env vars. You can also set a
# per-provider model with <PROVIDER>_MODEL (optional; sensible defaults apply).

# Google Gemini — aistudio.google.com/apikey  (GOOGLE_API_KEY is an alias)
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash           # or: PREP_VISION_MODEL (legacy alias)

# Anthropic (Claude) — console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5

# OpenAI — platform.openai.com/api-keys
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# --- Storage backend ------------------------------------------------------
# Force the evidence/catalog store. Leave unset to auto-detect: "cloudflare" on
# the Workers runtime, "file" (local data/ directory) on plain `next dev`.
# Values: file | cloudflare
# OPSCONSOLE_STORE=

# --- Build (advanced) -----------------------------------------------------
# Override Next.js build output dir (used by the OpenNext/Cloudflare build).
# NEXT_DIST_DIR=.next

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloudflare deployment note:
# D1 / R2 / KV are supplied to the Worker as BINDINGS (see wrangler.jsonc), not
# as env vars here. Set production provider keys as Worker secrets instead:
#   wrangler secret put GEMINI_API_KEY
#   wrangler secret put ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
#   wrangler secret put OPENAI_API_KEY
